            src={ogImageUrl}
            alt={ogAltText}
            width="1200"
            height="675"
            class="w-full h-full object-cover"
            loading="eager"
            fetchpriority="high"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>

        {/* Verified Host E-E-A-T Attribution Bar */}
        <div class="bg-[#FAF9F6] p-4 sm:p-5 rounded-sm border border-[#EAE8E3] flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3.5">
            <img
              src="/images/Gaurav-pandey-casa-de-bello.webp"
              alt="Gaurav Pandey"
              class="w-11 h-11 rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-[#8A6F4A] shrink-0"
              width="44"
              height="44"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <div>
              <span class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#7A6038] block">Verified Local Host &amp; Operational Advisory</span>
              <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm font-bold text-[#0E2C21]">Curated by Gaurav Pandey — Resident Director at Whispering Pines Resort</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 font-light">Malla Ramgarh (22 km / ~45 min from Kainchi Dham) • Direct WhatsApp: +91 75050 29696</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <a
            href={waDarshanLink}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="shrink-0 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-2.5 bg-[#25D366] hover:bg-[#1EBE5D] text-white font-bold text-xs rounded-sm shadow-sm transition-all"
          >
            <span>💬 Ask Front Desk on WhatsApp</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        {/* Share Bar Top */}
        <BlogShareBar
          title={pageTitle}
          url={canonicalUrl}
          description={pageDescription}
          label="Planning a family darshan to Kainchi Dham? Share this practical guide with your group"
          className="my-4"
        />

        {/* AEO Quick Answer Box */}
        <div class="aeo-direct-answer bg-[#FAF9F6] p-6 sm:p-7 rounded-sm border-l-4 border-[#8A6F4A] shadow-xs space-y-3">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#7A6038] block">
            Kainchi Dham Stay &amp; Darshan in 2026: Quick Executive Answer
          </span>
          <p class="text-base text-gray-800 leading-relaxed font-light">
            <strong>If you are searching for a peaceful hotel near Kainchi Dham with verified parking and senior-friendly comfort, staying in Malla Ramgarh (22 km / 45–50 min drive) is the most reliable strategy.</strong> On weekends, private vehicles are stopped at Bhowali or Bhimtal intercept lots where shuttle buses take devotees to the temple. By basing your family at Whispering Pines Resort, you escape the highway gridlock, wake up to 180° Himalayan snow peaks, enjoy Satvik dining, and reach the ashram in under 45 minutes on weekday mornings.
          </p>
          <div class="pt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-xs text-[#0E2C21] font-medium">
            <span>✓ No Registration Required (Nov 2026)</span>
            <span>✓ Flat 25% Direct Booking Discount</span>
            <span>✓ Free On-Site Parking for 25+ Cars</span>
            <span>✓ Ground-Floor Step-Free Rooms</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        {/* Article Body Content */}
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-[#2C3531] font-light leading-relaxed prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-[#0E2C21] prose-a:text-[#0E2C21] prose-a:font-semibold prose-a:underline space-y-8">
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
            Over the Gandhi Jayanti weekend in October 2026, more than 50,000 devotees reached Kainchi Dham. The Nainital district administration has since urged visitors to arrange their accommodation beforehand instead of searching for rooms on arrival along the packed highway corridor. If you are bringing parents, grandparents or small children to Neem Karoli Baba's ashram, the scenic mountain drive is not the challenge — navigating the weekend parking rules, shuttle buses, and morning temple queues is.
          </p>

          <p>
            This guide breaks down how Kainchi Dham parking and shuttles operate right now, current registration requirements, and the step-by-step darshan schedule we recommend to families staying at <a href="/about-whispering-pines-resort-ramgarh/">Whispering Pines Resort</a> — our 25-room boutique 4-star property and standalone 10-guest Alpine Villa located 22 km away on the quiet fruit orchards of the Malla Ramgarh ridge.
          </p>

          {/* Section 1: Parking & Shuttle Rules */}
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#0E2C21] pt-6 border-t border-gray-100">
            Kainchi Dham Parking and Shuttle Rules in 2026
          </h2>

          <p>
            <strong>On Saturdays, Sundays, and major religious festivals, police stop private cars at designated outlying parking lots — primarily Bhowali Sanatorium and Bhimtal Vikas Bhawan — and devotees board official shuttle vehicles to reach the shrine. Taxis and two-wheelers are also strictly barred from the inner temple approach on weekends. On weekdays, private cars can usually drive to the ashram, though parking space near the main bridge remains scarce after 8:30 AM.</strong>
          </p>

          <p>
            Traffic protocols in the Nainital hills are dynamically reviewed each week. Since October 2026, administrative officers at the SDM, CO (Circle Officer), and ARTO levels convene prior to every weekend to finalize parking allocations, shuttle fleets, and one-way diversions based on projected crowd counts. Here is how the system currently functions:
          </p>

          {/* Table 1: Parking & Shuttle Matrix */}
          <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6 border border-[#EAE8E3] rounded-sm bg-white shadow-xs">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm text-[#2C3531]">
              <thead class="bg-[#0E2C21] text-[#FAF9F6] text-xs uppercase font-semibold">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3.5">Day Type</th>
                  <th class="p-3.5">Can Private Cars Reach Ashram?</th>
                  <th class="p-3.5">Where You Must Park</th>
                  <th class="p-3.5">Shuttle Service &amp; Fare</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 text-xs sm:text-sm">
                <tr class="hover:bg-[#FAF9F6]/60">
                  <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-[#0E2C21]">Regular Weekdays (Mon – Fri)</td>
                  <td class="p-3.5">Yes, permitted subject to available roadside bay capacity.</td>
                  <td class="p-3.5">Designated roadside parking bays near Kainchi; overflow directed to Bhowali.</td>
                  <td class="p-3.5">Runs 8:00 AM to 2:00 PM when needed (~₹20–₹30 per head).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="hover:bg-[#FAF9F6]/60 bg-amber-50/30">
                  <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-[#0E2C21]">Saturdays, Sundays &amp; Long Weekends</td>
                  <td class="p-3.5 text-red-700 font-semibold">No private cars or commercial cabs permitted past checkpoints.</td>
                  <td class="p-3.5">Bhowali Sanatorium ground (from Ramgarh / Nainital) or Bhimtal Vikas Bhawan lot.</td>
                  <td class="p-3.5 font-medium">Continuous shuttle fleets operate 7:00 AM to 8:00 PM (~₹20–₹30 one-way).</td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="hover:bg-[#FAF9F6]/60">
                  <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-[#0E2C21]">Kainchi Dham Foundation Day (15 June)</td>
                  <td class="p-3.5 text-red-700 font-semibold">Strict total vehicle freeze (typically 13 to 16 June).</td>
                  <td class="p-3.5">Mass peripheral parking lots at Haldwani, Kathgodam, Bhimtal &amp; Bhowali.</td>
                  <td class="p-3.5">Mass shuttle operations running continuously round the clock.</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-[#FAF9F6] p-5 rounded-sm border-l-4 border-[#B0966D] my-4">
            <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-[#0E2C21] mb-1">What this means when staying in Malla Ramgarh:</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-700 font-light leading-relaxed">
              When travelling from Whispering Pines Resort in Malla Ramgarh, you take the scenic descent to Bhowali junction. On a weekday at 7:00 AM, the Bhowali-Kainchi road is breezy and completely clear, allowing you to reach the shrine in roughly 45 minutes. On a Saturday or Sunday, you simply park your car at the designated Bhowali Sanatorium grounds and take the short 10-minute shuttle ride down. Our front desk verifies the evening before exactly which lot is operational for the following morning.
            </p>
          </div>

          {/* Section 2: Registration Rules */}
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#0E2C21] pt-6 border-t border-gray-100">
            Do You Need Online Registration for Kainchi Dham Darshan?
          </h2>

          <p>
            <strong>No online registration, token system, or pre-booking pass is required for Kainchi Dham darshan as of November 2026.</strong> Entry to Neem Karoli Baba Ashram remains 100% free for all devotees.
          </p>

          <p>
            Following unprecedented holiday crowds exceeding 50,000 visitors over single weekends, district officials proposed evaluating a tourist registration framework modelled on the Uttarakhand Char Dham Yatra. However, no official notification or portal cap has been put into effect. If an official registration system is ever introduced by the administration, our front desk team will update this guide immediately.
          </p>

          {/* Section 3: The Family Darshan Plan */}
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#0E2C21] pt-6 border-t border-gray-100">
            The Family Darshan Plan We Recommend for Elders &amp; Kids
          </h2>

          <p>
            The itinerary that exhausts senior family members is the one frequently promoted online: driving through the night from Delhi or Lucknow, reaching Bhowali around 10:00 AM on a crowded Saturday, and standing directly in a 2-hour queue under the sun.
          </p>

          <p>
            The serene, respectful way to experience Kainchi Dham takes just one extra night:
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-4 my-6">
            <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-sm border border-[#EAE8E3] shadow-xs">
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[#0E2C21]">Day 1 — Relaxed Afternoon Arrival &amp; Peak Views</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-light mt-1">
                Arrive at Whispering Pines Resort by 2:00 PM. Let elderly parents unpack and rest in peaceful, heated mountain rooms. Sip fresh orchard tea on the 2,200 sq ft lawn facing the snow peaks of Nanda Devi and Trishul. Enjoy an early, comforting Satvik dinner and retire early.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-sm border border-[#EAE8E3] shadow-xs">
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[#0E2C21]">Day 2 (Preferred Weekday) — Early Sunrise Darshan</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-light mt-1">
                Enjoy hot morning tea delivered to your suite at 6:15 AM. Depart the resort at 6:45 AM. Reach the ashram by 7:30 AM before outside tourist traffic arrives. Experience heartfelt darshan in the morning quiet, receive Baba Neem Karoli's blessed prasad, and return to the resort by 10:00 AM for a hot breakfast buffet.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-sm border border-[#EAE8E3] shadow-xs">
              <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-[#0E2C21]">Day 2 Afternoon — Pure Relaxation</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-light mt-1">
                No rushed driving. Rest in the crisp mountain air, stroll through the organic apple and peach orchards of Ramgarh, or gather for a warm evening bonfire with live barbecue counters under starlit skies.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="bg-[#FAF9F6] p-4 rounded-sm border-l-2 border-[#7A6038] my-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-gray-700 font-light">
            <strong>Planning a longer Kumaon holiday?</strong> If you are combining your pilgrimage with Naini Lake boating and Mukteshwar cliff views, explore our complete <a href="/blog/nainital-itinerary/" class="text-[#0E2C21] font-semibold underline">3-Day Nainital, Kainchi Dham &amp; Mukteshwar Itinerary</a> to see how staying in Malla Ramgarh connects all three destinations in under an hour each way.
          </div>

          {/* Darshan Morning Schedule Table */}
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#0E2C21] pt-2">Recommended Morning Darshan Timeline</h3>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4 border border-[#EAE8E3] rounded-sm bg-white shadow-xs">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm text-[#2C3531]">
              <thead class="bg-[#7A6038] text-white text-xs uppercase font-semibold">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-3">Time</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Action</th>
                  <th class="p-3">Devotee Advantage</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 text-xs sm:text-sm">
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-[#0E2C21]">6:15 AM</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Freshly brewed herbal or ginger tea served to your suite.</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Warms elders before the crisp morning drive.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-[#0E2C21]">6:45 AM</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Depart Whispering Pines Resort via Ramgarh-Bhowali Rd.</td>
                  <td class="p-3">Roads are completely empty; pristine mountain views.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td class="p-3 font-bold text-[#0E2C21]">7:30 AM</td>
